{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129772",
      "title": "Adding Validators To Reactive Forms",
      "lectureOrder": 254,
      "videoOrder": 242,
      "sourceHash": "260e975b310065e3fd25a25ed69a751ae35862fc51b72bbddf2bcf5530b97634",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 2.46,
          "en": "So, how can we make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.46,
          "end": 7.46,
          "en": "that these inputs here are validated by Angular?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.83,
          "end": 10.77,
          "en": "Now, when using the template driven approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.77,
          "end": 14.1,
          "en": "we ensure the validation by adding attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.1,
          "end": 17.52,
          "en": "or directives in the end like required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.52,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "to our input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 23.82,
          "en": "When using the reactive forms approach, we don't do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.82,
          "end": 25.77,
          "en": "Instead there, the idea really",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.77,
          "end": 28.5,
          "en": "is that we set up everything in our code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.5,
          "end": 30.36,
          "en": "in our TypeScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 33.87,
          "en": "And therefore, you add validators to form controls.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.87,
          "end": 37.11,
          "en": "Here, when you create those controls,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.11,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "though you could also add validators later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 41.34,
          "en": "by accessing the forum,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 44.94,
          "en": "and then you could access a control like the email control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.94,
          "end": 47.64,
          "en": "and call add validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.64,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "If you needed to add more dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 52.17,
          "en": "at some point in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.17,
          "end": 55.08,
          "en": "This is a more advanced use case though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.08,
          "end": 59.01,
          "en": "Instead, in most cases, you probably want to add validators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 60.84,
          "en": "when the form is being created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.84,
          "end": 64.26,
          "en": "and you can easily do that by adding a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.26,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "to your form control constructor here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 71.425,
          "en": "And that second argument could be an array of validators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.425,
          "end": 72.994,
          "en": "and I'll show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.994,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "what a validator looks like in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 80.91,
          "en": "But it can alternatively also be a configuration object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.91,
          "end": 82.98,
          "en": "which is the approach I'll use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.98,
          "end": 85.337,
          "en": "since it's a bit more descriptive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.337,
          "end": 88.41,
          "en": "because this configuration object now, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.41,
          "end": 93.41,
          "en": "takes a validator key to register this array of validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.11,
          "end": 95.78999999999999,
          "en": "And I think that's simply a bit easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.78999999999999,
          "end": 97.263,
          "en": "to read and understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.25,
          "end": 100.89,
          "en": "Now, you could also add asyncValidators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 102.75,
          "en": "and I'll get back to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.75,
          "end": 104.49000000000001,
          "en": "You could make sure that this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.49000000000001,
          "end": 109.43,
          "en": "can't be set to null again if it were reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.43,
          "end": 114.43,
          "en": "And you can also control if the value managed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.93,
          "end": 116.94,
          "en": "should update on every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.94,
          "end": 121.68,
          "en": "or only if the input loses focus with updateOn.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.68,
          "end": 124.353,
          "en": "But here, I only care about the validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.22,
          "end": 129.6,
          "en": "And a validator in the end is a function, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.6,
          "end": 130.74,
          "en": "And we will later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.74,
          "end": 135.66,
          "en": "also build our own validator in this section here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.66,
          "end": 139.47,
          "en": "For the moment, we'll use a built-in validator instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 142.982,
          "en": "And we can do that by using the validator's object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.982,
          "end": 146.913,
          "en": "which is imported from @angular/forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "So, this import must be added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 153.24,
          "en": "And this validators object here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.24,
          "end": 158.24,
          "en": "this class in the end then has some validators it exposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 160.92000000000002,
          "en": "Like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.92000000000002,
          "end": 164.79,
          "en": "the email validator for this email control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.79,
          "end": 165.87,
          "en": "And this will ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.87,
          "end": 169.47,
          "en": "that Angular checks whether a valid email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.47,
          "end": 170.703,
          "en": "has been entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.66,
          "end": 174.51,
          "en": "In addition, we can use the required validator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 176.597,
          "en": "to make sure that it's not empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.597,
          "end": 181.597,
          "en": "And for the password, I'll also register validators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.13,
          "end": 187.13,
          "en": "And there, I want to make sure that it is required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 191.733,
          "en": "and that it has a main length of six characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.57,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "And of course you can play around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 196.92000000000002,
          "en": "with the other validators here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.92000000000002,
          "end": 198.18,
          "en": "And as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.18,
          "end": 201.87,
          "en": "we'll also create our own validator function later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.87,
          "end": 206.103,
          "en": "For the moment, these are the validators I want to add here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.94,
          "end": 208.26,
          "en": "With those added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.26,
          "end": 212.64,
          "en": "Angular will keep track of the control validity status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 215.37,
          "en": "and the overall form validity status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.37,
          "end": 219.69,
          "en": "just as it did before with the template-driven approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.69,
          "end": 222.69,
          "en": "Therefore, we can of course also output an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.69,
          "end": 225.36,
          "en": "if invalid values have been entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 225.36,
          "end": 230.36,
          "en": "So, we can add this if check again and now use our form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.505,
          "end": 233.16,
          "en": "And there, the controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 237.03,
          "en": "and check if email was touched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.03,
          "end": 241.47,
          "en": "and a form.controls.email is dirty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.47,
          "end": 245.261,
          "en": "So, if the user did also enter at least one character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.261,
          "end": 249.633,
          "en": "and if form.controls.email is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.47,
          "end": 253.5,
          "en": "And if all these conditions here are met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 253.5,
          "end": 257.76,
          "en": "we can output this paragraph with a CSS class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 257.76,
          "end": 262.113,
          "en": "of control-error where we could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.1,
          "end": 267.993,
          "en": "Please enter a valid email address or something like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.92,
          "end": 273.12,
          "en": "Now, of course this here is quite a lot of code to write,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.12,
          "end": 276.65999999999997,
          "en": "so therefore what you would often do is grab that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.65999999999997,
          "end": 279.783,
          "en": "and add a getter to your login component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 281.19,
          "end": 285.99,
          "en": "emailIsInvalid could be the getter name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.99,
          "end": 287.97,
          "en": "And then there, I would return,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 287.97,
          "end": 291.54,
          "en": "this.form.controls.email.touched,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 291.54,
          "end": 294.12,
          "en": "this.form.controls.email.dirty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.12,
          "end": 298.08,
          "en": "and this.form.controls.email.invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 298.08,
          "end": 302.55,
          "en": "And with that, I outsourced this check here into this getter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 302.55,
          "end": 303.99,
          "en": "and in the log in component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 303.99,
          "end": 307.71,
          "en": "I can use this emailIsInvalid getter property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 307.71,
          "end": 309.75,
          "en": "in my if check now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 309.75,
          "end": 312.63,
          "en": "We can also duplicate this getter now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.63,
          "end": 314.881,
          "en": "and set up a getter for the password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 314.881,
          "end": 319.881,
          "en": "and check if this form.controls.password is touched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 320.1,
          "end": 322.023,
          "en": "and dirty and invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 323.07,
          "end": 325.35,
          "en": "And with that added, back in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 325.35,
          "end": 328.755,
          "en": "we can duplicate this if check and this error paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 328.755,
          "end": 332.55,
          "en": "and use our passwordIsInvalid getter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 332.55,
          "end": 336.39,
          "en": "to output Please enter a valid password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 336.39,
          "end": 339.363,
          "en": "at least 6 characters long.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 340.56,
          "end": 342.84000000000003,
          "en": "With that, this is all updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 342.84000000000003,
          "end": 344.13,
          "en": "And if we go back now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.13,
          "end": 346.38,
          "en": "you'll see initially I see no error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 346.38,
          "end": 348.33,
          "en": "and no error styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 348.33,
          "end": 352.32,
          "en": "But if I tap into here, type at least one character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 352.32,
          "end": 355.53,
          "en": "and go out of here, you see now it's marked as invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 355.53,
          "end": 357.205,
          "en": "from a styling perspective",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 357.205,
          "end": 359.94,
          "en": "and we have this error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 359.94,
          "end": 362.22,
          "en": "And we got this error styling here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 362.22,
          "end": 364.08,
          "en": "because just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 364.08,
          "end": 367.83,
          "en": "Angular adds these special classes to these inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 367.83,
          "end": 370.23,
          "en": "So, that works just as before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 370.23,
          "end": 373.038,
          "en": "with the template-driven approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 373.038,
          "end": 375.06,
          "en": "And hence here, I can now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 375.06,
          "end": 378.338,
          "en": "of course also enter a valid email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 378.338,
          "end": 382.593,
          "en": "And for the password, I also got some validation going on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 383.61,
          "end": 386.25,
          "en": "So, that's there for all looking good",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 386.25,
          "end": 390.3,
          "en": "and working the way it should now with help of validators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 390.3,
          "end": 394.023,
          "en": "that are added by using this reactive forms approach.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
